    ``axes (0, 1)`` will be ``(2, 3)`` and dimension along other axes will be
    same as that of input.

    >>> with jnp.printoptions(precision=2, suppress=True):
    ...   jnp.fft.irfft2(x, s=[2, 3], axes=(0, 1))
    Array([[[ 4.67,  6.67,  8.67],
            [-0.33, -0.33, -0.33],
            [-0.33, -0.33, -0.33]],
    <BLANKLINE>
           [[-3.  , -3.  , -3.  ],
            [ 0.  ,  0.  ,  0.  ],
            [ 0.  ,  0.  ,  0.  ]]], dtype=float32)

